cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "measureRAG: a budget-aware retrieval and RAG benchmark in Czech and English, for a single machine with no network access"
abstract: >-
  measureRAG is a budget-aware benchmark for retrieval and retrieval-augmented
  generation on a single CPU-only machine with no network access, in Czech and
  English. It imposes a deployment budget of memory and latency first and
  reports answer quality inside it, and it asks whether the next gigabyte buys
  more as a stronger retriever or as a bigger generator. On HotpotQA and Natural
  Questions the answer is a break-even gold-gain table rather than a located
  crossover, and Czech retrieval and Czech RAG are measured alongside.
